s name, its type and its quantifier (\"\", \"?\", \"*\")."] [241 1 "// astCon is a constructor of a sum (sum its sum's name) or a product type (sum \"\")."] [248 1 "// astSum is a sum type: its attributes and constructors; simple when no constructor has a field."] [258 27 "// constructors of sums and products, by name"] [259 27 "// the _ast module's classes, by name"] [272 1 "// astSchemaOf is the schema of astTable with the module's classes (the module imported first)."] [314 1 "// astNode is a node of the C level's tree: its constructor's (or product's) name and its fields' values: nil (NULL),"] [315 1 "// *astNode, []any (a sequence), Object (identifier, string, constant) or int; pos its attributes when it has some."] [353 1 "// obj2ast converts obj, a value of the asdl type typ (obj2ast_TYPE)."] [415 1 "// field converts the field f of obj for owner (the node's name in the messages)."] [460 1 "// attrs reads the position attributes (the optional ends default to the starts)."] [489 1 "// fields reads a constructor's fields, then checks its required ones as the C constructor (_PyAST_NAME) does."] [569 1 "// astObj2Mod is PyAST_obj2mod: the mode's node checked (PyAst_CheckMode), then converted."] [591 1 "// ---- Python/ast.c: _PyAST_Validate ----"] [1334 1 "// astValidate is _PyAST_Validate."] [1351 1 "// ---- PyAST_mod2obj ----"] [1353 1 "// ast2obj makes x, a value of the asdl type typ, objects again (ast2obj_TYPE): a node of the _ast module's class with"] [1354 1 "// every field and attribute set."] [1396 1 "// compileASTObject is compile()'s branch for an AST object: with PyCF_ONLY_AST the converted, validated and"] [1397 1 "// preprocessed tree as objects; else the validated tree's text (ast.unparse) for the compiler."] [1417 1 "// The AST's preprocessing (queue 202c; Python/ast_preprocess.c, _PyAST_Preprocess, as compile() runs it for"] [1418 1 "// PyCF_ONLY_AST): with PyCF_OPTIMIZED_AST (ast.parse's optimize > 0) the folding: __debug__ a constant, a str's %"